  | [SetError], [§5.3] | [proto_error.ml] | {!Jmap.Proto.Method.set_failures} gathers the [notCreated], [notUpdated] and [notDestroyed] entries of a response, {!Jmap.Proto.Method.pp_set_failure} prints one of them and {!Jmap.Proto.Error.Set_error.pp} prints the error alone | [test/method/test_method.ml] ("pp_set_failure") | [test/oracle/email/test_email.ml] | [examples/7-keywords/], [examples/k-compose/], [examples/9-errors/] |
}

