{2 Client behaviour}

The client layer of [eio/] is not a method table, but the RFC has as much to
say about it. It fixes what a client may send, how often, and what it must do
when the session changes underneath.

{t
  | Feature | Where | Unit test | Oracle test | Example |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | Sending a chain, [§3.2] | {!Jmap_eio.Client.val-call} for a chain ending in one handle, {!Jmap_eio.Client.run} for one ending in several, {!Jmap_eio.Client.run_with_response} for the responses and the raw response together, {!Jmap_eio.Client.chain} for the response itself | [test/eio/test_eio.ml] ("call decodes the one handle", "call reports a method error", "run reads a two handle chain", "run_with_response keeps the response") | all suites | [examples/2-mailboxes/] ([call_exn] and [chain_exn]), [examples/3-inbox/] ([run_exn]), [examples/k-compose/] ([run_with_response_exn]), every later example |
  | Credential schemes: bearer (RFC 6750 [§2.1]), basic (RFC 7617), from a file, from a thunk, from the environment | {!Jmap_eio.Auth} | [test/eio/test_auth.ml] ("auth": each scheme on the wire, [of_env], redaction by [pp]) | [test/oracle/smoke/test_smoke.ml] ("connect with basic auth", "connect with a key file") | every example, via [Cli.auth_value] |
  | Shared named connection profiles | {!Jmap_eio.Profile} ({!Jmap_eio.Profile.load}, {!Jmap_eio.Profile.list}, {!Jmap_eio.Profile.save}, {!Jmap_eio.Profile.connect_name}); {!Jmap_eio.Cli.profile_term} | [test/eio/test_profile.ml] (validation including controls, XDG location, permissions, bounded atomic replacement, selected-profile connection); [mosaic/test/test_login.ml] (legacy migration); {!page-profiles} (mdx) | — | [examples/0-profiles/] (save, list, connect); every connected example via [--profile]; [jmap-mosaic] profile picker |
  | Credential scoping to the session's origins, [§2] | [eio/client.ml] | [test/eio/test_eio.ml] (in-scope and out-of-scope hosts), [test/eio/test_auth.ml] | [test/oracle/smoke/test_smoke.ml] | every example |
  | HTTP stack: TLS trust anchors, retries, cookies, per-origin pacing | {!Jmap_eio.Transport} | [test/eio/test_auth.ml] ("transport": [of_fetch], missing clock); [test/eio/test_eio.ml] (cookie origin matching and persistent file mode) | used by every oracle suite | every example |
  | Per-exchange timeout | {!Jmap_eio.Client.connect} [?timeout] → [Client.Timeout] | [test/eio/test_auth.ml] (a slow server times out; [?timeout] without a clock is [Invalid_argument]); [mosaic/test/test_login.ml] (Mosaic timeout) | [test/oracle/smoke/test_smoke.ml] ("connect times out") | [jmap-mosaic] |
  | Transport failures as values ([Client.Transport of Fetch.error * string]) | [eio/client.ml] | [test/eio/test_eio.ml] | — | every example, via [Client.error_to_string] |
  | Session lifecycle: [sessionState] mismatch refetches the session, [§2] and [§3.4] | [eio/client.ml] ({!Jmap_eio.Client.refresh_session}, {!Jmap_eio.Client.on_session_change}, {!Jmap_eio.Client.session_changed}) | [test/eio/test_client2.ml] ("session state": one refetch under concurrency, a lagging session resource, broadcast, a raising observer) | [test/oracle/smoke/test_smoke.ml] | — |
  | [maxConcurrentRequests] / [maxConcurrentUpload], [§2] | [eio/client.ml] ({!Jmap_eio.Client.concurrency_limits}) | [test/eio/test_client2.ml] ("concurrency limits": limits from the capability, absent and zero default, requests and uploads bounded separately) | [test/oracle/email/test_email.ml] ("eight chains at once") | — |
  | [maxSizeRequest] / [maxSizeUpload], [§2] | {!Jmap_eio.Client.request}, {!Jmap_eio.Client.upload}, {!Jmap_eio.Client.upload_flow} | [test/eio/test_eio.ml] ("session request and upload limits") | — | [examples/p-stream/] reads the upload limit before opening the file |
  | [position]/[limit] paging, [§5.5] | {!Jmap_eio.Sync.pages}, {!Jmap_eio.Sync.all_ids} | [test/eio/test_eio.ml] (server limit, short and empty pages, changed query state, non-advancing page, request fuel, collection cap) | [test/oracle/sync/test_sync.ml] ("Sync.pages walks the inbox") | [examples/h-search/], [examples/d-paging/] |
  | Draining [hasMoreChanges], [§5.2], and [cannotCalculateChanges] as a value | {!Jmap_eio.Sync.val-changes}, [email_changes], [mailbox_changes], [thread_changes] | [test/eio/test_eio.ml] (multi-round folding, finite fuel, repeated states, method errors, [cannotCalculateChanges]) | [test/oracle/sync/test_sync.ml] ("Sync.email_changes since a state") | [examples/n-resync/], [examples/e-changes/] |
  | Batching a [/get] over [maxObjectsInGet], [§5.1] | {!Jmap_eio.Sync.get_all} | [test/eio/test_eio.ml] (ordering, concurrency, failure stop, empty ids and a zero server limit) | [test/oracle/sync/test_sync.ml] ("Sync.get_all batches by two") | [examples/h-search/], [examples/d-paging/] |
  | [maxCallsInRequest] as a bound on a chain, [§2] | {!Jmap_eio.Client.request}, {!Jmap_eio.Sync.calls_in_chain}, {!Jmap_eio.Sync.chain_fits} | [test/eio/test_eio.ml] (local rejection, chain counting, one-call mailbox fallback) | — | — |
}

